{%- comment -%}
  MIGRATION-DEBT: bd hairmnl-theme-ioba.1 (2026-08-25). Reward-gift checkout
  safeguards — two Micromodal dialogs, markup only. Behaviour lives in
  assets/hairmnl-common.js section 11.

  Rendered once from layout/theme.liquid before </body>, gated on the two
  settings, so with both switched off this file emits nothing at all and the
  JS section self-disables (it looks for these element ids).

  Copy approved by the team in the feasibility doc, 2026-08-25. Strings live in
  locales/en.default.json under cart.general.reward_* so ops can retitle without
  a deploy.

  Port to OS 2.0: copy this snippet + the theme.liquid render line + JS
  section 11. No Pipeline-6 coupling beyond themeVendor.MicroModal and the
  theme:cart:change event. Audit row in
  os2-migration/customization-audit.md "Recent additions".
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  # Shared by BOTH modals (independent settings, so computed once up here).
  # Falls back reward_gate_offers_url -> cart_continue_browsing -> all-products,
  # so a blank setting can never render a dead link.
  assign rg_offers_url = settings.reward_gate_offers_url
  if rg_offers_url == blank
    assign rg_offers_url = settings.cart_continue_browsing
  endif
  if rg_offers_url == blank
    assign rg_offers_url = routes.all_products_collection_url
  endif
-%}

{%- if settings.reward_reminder_enabled -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Post-redemption reminder. Shown once per redemption when a reward gift
    newly lands in the cart. Team constraint (Vikky, 2026-08-25): this must
    never close or cover LoyaltyLion's own voucher-code window — section 11
    holds it until that window is gone. Our DOM is entirely separate from
    LL's, so we cannot close theirs even by accident.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div
    class="modal micromodal-slide"
    id="reward-reminder-modal"
    data-modal
    aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal__overlay" tabindex="-1" data-micromodal-close>
      <button
        data-micromodal-close
        class="modal__close"
        aria-label="{{ 'cart.general.close_cart' | t }}">
      </button>
      <div
        class="modal__container modal__container--inline"
        data-modal-content
        role="dialog"
        aria-modal="true"
        aria-labelledby="reward-reminder-title">
        <div class="modal__content">
          <h3 id="reward-reminder-title">{{ 'cart.general.reward_reminder_title' | t }}</h3>
          {%- comment -%}
            Team feedback (Basecamp, 2026-09-07): the reminder also fires when a
            regular paid item is already in the cart (by design — the trigger is
            "a reward newly landed"), and "please add a paid item" reads wrong
            then. Two bodies; section 11 shows the right one at fire time from
            the cart payload. The has-paid one is hidden server-side so a
            JS-less render still shows only the original approved copy.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <p data-reminder-body="no-paid">{{ 'cart.general.reward_reminder_body' | t }}</p>
          <p data-reminder-body="has-paid" hidden style="display:none">{{ 'cart.general.reward_reminder_body_has_paid' | t }}</p>
          {%- comment -%}
            Team decision (Basecamp, 2026-08-26): the reminder also carries the
            "Complete your order" CTA. Same label + destination as the gate
            modal, so ops edit one setting/locale key and both stay in step.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Actions wrapper (team revisions, 2026-08-26): side-by-side on
            desktop, stacked on mobile. Styling in css-overrides.source.liquid.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="reward-modal__actions">
            <a
              href="{{ rg_offers_url }}"
              class="btn btn--primary uppercase reward-modal__primary">
              {{ 'cart.general.reward_gate_cta' | t }}
            </a>
            <button
              type="button"
              class="btn uppercase reward-modal__secondary"
              data-micromodal-close>
              {{ 'cart.general.reward_reminder_continue' | t }}
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if settings.reward_multi_gate_enabled -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    "Rewards are not stackable" explainer (bd hairmnl-theme-582o, 2026-09-11).
    Opened by section 11 when the cart holds more than one reward gift —
    including when regular paid items are present, which the reward-only gate
    deliberately allows through.

    Why this exists: the LoyaltyLion voucher discounts ONE reward. A team
    screenshot showed a cart with a reward line at QUANTITY 5 plus another
    reward line; the voucher took P9,999 off P49,995, leaving the shopper
    charged P39,996 for products meant to be free.

    Only a dismiss button: the fix is removing the extra rewards, which the
    shopper does in the cart they are already looking at. No offers CTA —
    sending them to buy more would be the wrong instruction here.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div
    class="modal micromodal-slide"
    id="reward-multi-modal"
    data-modal
    aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal__overlay" tabindex="-1" data-micromodal-close>
      <button
        data-micromodal-close
        class="modal__close"
        aria-label="{{ 'cart.general.close_cart' | t }}">
      </button>
      <div
        class="modal__container modal__container--inline"
        data-modal-content
        role="dialog"
        aria-modal="true"
        aria-labelledby="reward-multi-title">
        <div class="modal__content">
          <h3 id="reward-multi-title">{{ 'cart.general.reward_multi_title' | t }}</h3>
          <p>{{ 'cart.general.reward_multi_body' | t }}</p>
          <div class="reward-modal__actions">
            <button
              type="button"
              class="btn btn--primary uppercase reward-modal__primary"
              data-micromodal-close>
              {{ 'cart.general.reward_multi_close' | t }}
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if settings.reward_gate_enabled -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Reward-only checkout explainer. Opened by section 11 when a shopper taps a
    checkout button whose cart contains nothing but reward gifts.

    The CTA falls back through settings.reward_gate_offers_url ->
    settings.cart_continue_browsing -> all-products, so a blank setting can
    never render a dead link.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div
    class="modal micromodal-slide"
    id="reward-gate-modal"
    data-modal
    aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal__overlay" tabindex="-1" data-micromodal-close>
      <button
        data-micromodal-close
        class="modal__close"
        aria-label="{{ 'cart.general.close_cart' | t }}">
      </button>
      <div
        class="modal__container modal__container--inline"
        data-modal-content
        role="dialog"
        aria-modal="true"
        aria-labelledby="reward-gate-title">
        <div class="modal__content">
          <h3 id="reward-gate-title">{{ 'cart.general.reward_gate_title' | t }}</h3>
          <p>{{ 'cart.general.reward_gate_body' | t }}</p>
          <div class="reward-modal__actions">
            <a
              href="{{ rg_offers_url }}"
              class="btn btn--primary uppercase reward-modal__primary">
              {{ 'cart.general.reward_gate_cta' | t }}
            </a>
            <button
              type="button"
              class="btn uppercase reward-modal__secondary"
              data-micromodal-close>
              {{ 'cart.general.reward_gate_close' | t }}
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
